      "author_login": "samueldemoura",
      "content": "## Summary\n\nRequesting logprobs when running inference against a Gemma3-based model results in:\n\n```\nERROR:      File \"/run/media/user/root/Downloads/exllamav3/exllamav3/generator/job.py\", line 565, in receive_sample\nERROR:        self.held_logits.append(logits[:1, :, :])\nERROR:      File \"/run/media/user/root/Downloads/exllamav3/exllamav3/util/tensor.py\", line 73, in append\nERROR:        s.copy_(new_data)\nERROR:    RuntimeError: The size of tensor a (262208) must match the size of tensor b (262272) at non-singleton dimension 2\n```\n\n## Reproduction\n\nPretty easy to reproduce over tabbyAPI. A basic request works as expected:\n\n```shell\n# perfectly fine! API responds normally\ncurl -X POST $OPENAI_BASE_URL/v1/chat/completions \\\n              -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n              -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_API_KEY\" \\\n              -d '{\"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"}]}'\n```\n\nHowever, when requesting logprobs...\n\n```shell\n# no good\ncurl -X POST $OPENAI_BASE_URL/v1/chat/completions \\\n              -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n              -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OPENAI_API_KEY\" \\\n              -d '{\"logprobs\": true, \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"}]}'\n```\n\n...it fails with:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"detail\": \"Chat completion 4e0d21cef71241508d427758a16dda67 aborted. Maybe the model was unloaded? Please check the server console.\"\n}\n```\n\nAnd the server logs have the `RuntimeError` I pasted in the summary section above.\n\n## Details\n\nA quick `grep` for these dimensions shows that 262272 comes from the model's head - here's a copy-paste from the model's [quantization_config.json](https://huggingface.co/turboderp/gemma-3-27b-it-exl3/raw/4.0bpw/quantization_config.json):\n\n```json\n...\n        \"language_model.lm_head\": {\n            \"stored_tensors\": {\n                \"language_model.lm_head.suh\": {\n                    \"shape\": [\n                        5376\n                    ],\n                    \"n_bytes\": 10752,\n                    \"dtype\": \"torch.float16\"\n                },\n                \"language_model.lm_head.svh\": {\n                    \"shape\": [\n                        262272 // here!\n                    ],\n                    \"n_bytes\": 524544,\n                    \"dtype\": \"torch.float16\"\n                },\n...\n```\n\nAnd `262208` seems to come from the EXL3 library itself:\n\nhttps://github.com/turboderp-org/exllamav3/blob/56e9d038dee07aa1657b8febb7f6a259f7eda11c/exllamav3/models/gemma3.py#L24-L26\n\nGemini 2.5 Pro suggested that this might be caused by inconsistent padding multiples for vocab size vs. LM head (64 vs. 128), which seems likely, but I didn't dig into internals enough to check whether there might be anything else at play. Happy to share any more details if necessary.\n\n---\n\nP.S.: Thanks for the awesome work so far.",
